    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "tens to hundreds of megawatts? that feels way too low if we're talking about a structure that size. i mean, if you're trying to stabilize a 10^22 kg mass or maintain that specific resonance frequency against all the tidal stresses from earth, wouldn't the energy requirement be much, much higher?\n\ncan we try to be more precise with the math? if we treat the resonance as a continuous wave being driven by an internal mechanism to counteract gravitational decay, how would we calculate the minimum power output required to maintain that 1.56 Hz pulse? i want to see if the math pushes us into the terawatt or even petawatt range. \n\nif the math supports a massive energy requirement, it would explain why the thermal anomalies are so distinct. can you help me formulate an equation that links the resonance-driven stabilization to a power consumption value?",
      "source": "evaluator"
